{"ts":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"ea0711001f053e8a2786b159","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-ajj4r7","lineage:pm-ajj4r7","lineage:pm-usfg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-ajj4r7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-ajj4r7","lineage:pm-ajj4r7","lineage:pm-usfg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rncuf7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Annotation transposition recovery: detect pm <collection> add <id> before the item id is consumed as text"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub #979 reproduces a cross-collection agent grammar mistake: noun-verb-object input is parsed as id=add and text=<real item id>, then reported as a duplicate text-source collision. The refusal must recognize the resolvable item id, name the transposed subcommand, render role-labeled recovery data, and make the accepted --note alias discoverable or reject it. Duplicate check searched all statuses for notes add, transposed subcommand, annotation collision, item-id-as-text, and --note help; closed pm-185870 owns general unknown positional subcommands but not this annotation parser collision."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","annotations","area:cli","area:sdk","contracts","error-recovery","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"When an annotation collection receives id=add and its text positional resolves to a real item, the typed SDK/CLI refusal names the transposed subcommand and supplies the canonical pm <collection> <id> --add form; the machine-readable recovery bundle labels parsed positional roles rather than flattening them; notes, learnings, files, docs, comments, and test share the behavior; the accepted --note alias is declared in help/contracts or removed with a typed migration refusal; focused unit, integration, packaged npm/npx/bun/bunx acceptance, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, and docstring gates pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Turn a common annotation grammar transposition into a one-turn, machine-actionable recovery"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Avoid repeated failed agent turns and prevent normalized recovery receipts from obscuring positional roles"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"All annotation collections become safer and cheaper for agents to drive"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The defect reproduces on the latest immutable 2026.8.11 package and currently affects notes, learnings, files, docs, comments, and test workflows"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"GitHub #979"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7, 2026.8.10, and 2026.8.11; Node 22/26; Linux"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"In a temporary workspace with item tst-y0bb, run pm notes add tst-y0bb --note hello; observe id=add/text=tst-y0bb collision guidance instead of transposed-subcommand recovery"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A typed refusal says add is not an annotation subcommand, identifies tst-y0bb as the item id, and shows pm notes tst-y0bb --add hello"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The CLI reports that note text was supplied twice and emits a flat normalized_args receipt that hides which token filled each positional slot"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-185870","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-8nyc","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-a2h3","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-n7rr","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pbyu","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vcu7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ya7x55","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches over annotation transposition, notes add, positional subcommand, item-id-as-text, collision, and alias help found closed pm-185870, pm-vcu7, pm-a2h3, pm-8nyc and open grammar owners pm-n7rr/pm-ya7x55. Their full live metadata confirms none owns the resolvable-id transposition diagnosis or hidden --note alias. Canonical external report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-